        "problem": "Let $a=\u27e85,\\sqrt{2},0\u27e9$ and $b=\u27e8-1,1,0\u27e9.$ Find $a\\times b.$",
        "worked_solution": "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}5 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 1)i-(5\\cdot 0-0\\cdot (-1))j+(5\\cdot 1-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =0\\cdot i-0\\cdot j+(5+\\sqrt{2})k \\\\  & =\u27e80,0,5+\\sqrt{2}\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
